Postman

What is postman?
A tool to send requests receive respone and test Api end points of the server.

Why post man?
Because they want to verify whether an API works before connecting it to a frontend or another application.
Simple analogy : Think of a REST API as a waiter in a restaurant.
    Client → Customer
    REST API → Waiter
    Database → Kitchen
Normally, the customer orders through a menu (the frontend application).
With Postman, you're talking directly to the waiter, skipping the menu. You can ask for any operation (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) and immediately see the response.

What is Collections?
A Collection in Postman is a folder that stores related API requests.

For example, if you're building an Employee Management API, instead of keeping requests scattered, you group them into one collection.

Example:    Employee Management API (Collection)
            │
            ├── GET All Employees
            ├── GET Employee by ID
            ├── POST Add Employee
            ├── PUT Update Employee
            └── DELETE Employee

How do you create collection?
open postman
click the NEW(+) button
select the collection
Enter the collection name[EMA] , (Optional) Add a description such as : Collection for Employee CRUD REST APIs.

TYPES OF REQUCESTS:
| Request Name       | Method | URL                                 |
| ------------------ | ------ | ----------------------------------- |
| Get Employees      | GET    | `http://localhost:8080/employees`   |
| Get Employee by ID | GET    | `http://localhost:8080/employees/1` |
| Add Employee       | POST   | `http://localhost:8080/employees`   |
| Update Employee    | PUT    | `http://localhost:8080/employees/1` |
| Delete Employee    | DELETE | `http://localhost:8080/employees/1` |























